        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ਨਹਿਰ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਨਹਿਰ — nahir — \"a canal\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਸਾਡੇ ਪਿੰਡ ਦੇ ਨੇੜੇ ਨਹਿਰ ਹੈ। sāḍe piṇḍ de neṛe nahir hai. There is a canal near our village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਨਹਿਰ (nahir) is a loan, usually traced through Persian to Arabic nahr, \"river\"; its sense here, \"canal\", is a shift from that."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
